Feature: Backup and Vacuum Operations for customer_360_raw Table

  The system must efficiently back up the purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table as compressed parquet files partitioned by state, and perform a vacuum operation to retain only records from the last 30 days. All operations must be logged in purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log.

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.customer_360_raw
    And the backup parquet files must be stored in the Databricks volume at path "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"
    And the parquet files must use "snappy" compression codec
    And all columns from the source table must be included in the backup
    And the backup must be a full backup (all records)
    And the backup operation must precede the vacuum operation
    And the vacuum operation must be a hard delete, permanently removing old records
    And the backup and vacuum operations must be performed daily at 02:00 UTC
    And backup parquet files must be retained for 90 days in the volume
    And the script must have read access to purgo_playground.customer_360_raw and write access to /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup
    And all operations must be logged in purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log with timestamp, status, operation_type, record_count, and error_message

  Scenario: Successful full backup of customer_360_raw table to compressed parquet files partitioned by state
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table contains 100,000 records
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all 100,000 records are written to "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup" as parquet files
    And the parquet files are partitioned by the "state" column
    And the parquet files are compressed using "snappy"
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message |
      | SUCCESS | BACKUP        | 100000       | NULL          |

  Scenario: Successful vacuum operation retains only records from the last 30 days
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table contains records with creation_date ranging from 2024-03-01 to 2024-06-30
    And today is 2024-06-30
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then only records with creation_date >= 2024-05-31 are retained in purgo_playground.customer_360_raw
    And all records with creation_date < 2024-05-31 are permanently deleted
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message |
      | SUCCESS | VACUUM        | <remaining>  | NULL          |

  Scenario: Backup operation fails due to insufficient write permissions
    Given the script does not have write access to "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message                      |
      | FAILED  | BACKUP         | 0            | "Permission denied: write access"  |

  Scenario: Vacuum operation fails due to insufficient table permissions
    Given the script does not have delete permissions on purgo_playground.customer_360_raw
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then no records are deleted from purgo_playground.customer_360_raw
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message                      |
      | FAILED  | VACUUM         | 0            | "Permission denied: delete access" |

  Scenario: Backup operation fails due to storage quota exceeded
    Given the Databricks volume "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup" has less than 1GB free space
    And the backup size is estimated to be 10GB
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message                |
      | FAILED  | BACKUP         | 0            | "Insufficient storage space" |

  Scenario: Backup operation fails due to data validation error (invalid email format)
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table contains a record with email = "invalid-email-format"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup operation is aborted
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message                        |
      | FAILED  | BACKUP         | 0            | "Data validation error: invalid email format in record id=<id>" |

  Scenario Outline: Data validation for required fields before backup
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table contains a record with <column> = <invalid_value>
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup operation is aborted
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with
      | status  | operation_type | record_count | error_message                        |
      | FAILED  | BACKUP         | 0            | "Data validation error: <error_msg>" |
    Examples:
      | column     | invalid_value | error_msg                                 |
      | email      | NULL          | email is NULL in record id=<id>           |
      | id         | NULL          | id is NULL in record with email=<email>   |
      | state      | NULL          | state is NULL in record id=<id>           |

  Scenario: Parquet backup files are deleted after retention period
    Given a backup parquet file was created on 2024-03-01 in "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"
    And today is 2024-06-01
    When the retention policy job runs
    Then the backup parquet file from 2024-03-01 is deleted from "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"

  Scenario: Logging of all backup and vacuum operations
    Given a backup or vacuum operation is triggered
    When the operation completes (success or failure)
    Then a record is inserted into purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log with
      | timestamp          | status   | operation_type | record_count | error_message |
      | <ISO8601 datetime> | <status> | <BACKUP|VACUUM>| <count>      | <error>       |

  Scenario: Backup and vacuum operations are scheduled and executed daily at 02:00 UTC
    Given the current time is 02:00 UTC
    When the scheduled job runs
    Then the backup operation is performed
    And the vacuum operation is performed immediately after backup

  Scenario: Backup includes all columns from source table
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table has columns
      | id | name | email | phone | company | job_title | address | city | state | country | industry | account_manager | creation_date | last_interaction_date | purchase_history | notes | zip |
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the parquet files in "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup" contain all columns as above

  Scenario: Parquet files are partitioned by state
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table contains records with state values "CA", "NY", "TX"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the parquet files in "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup" are partitioned into directories
      | /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup/state=CA/ |
      | /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup/state=NY/ |
      | /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup/state=TX/ |

  Scenario: Parquet files are compressed using snappy
    Given the backup operation is triggered
    Then the resulting parquet files in "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup" use snappy compression

  Scenario: Only records from the last 30 days are retained after vacuum
    Given today is 2024-06-30
    And the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table contains records with creation_date from 2024-05-01 to 2024-06-30
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then only records with creation_date >= 2024-05-31 are retained

  Scenario: Error is logged if backup log table is unavailable
    Given the purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log table is unavailable
    When the backup or vacuum operation is triggered
    Then the operation fails
    And an error is raised: "Backup log table unavailable"

  Scenario: Backup and vacuum operations are atomic and do not leave partial state
    Given the backup operation is in progress
    And a failure occurs before completion
    Then no partial parquet files are left in "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with status "FAILED"

  Scenario: Backup and vacuum operations are idempotent
    Given the backup and vacuum operations are triggered multiple times within the same day
    When the operations run
    Then only one backup and one vacuum are performed per day
    And duplicate log entries are not created for the same operation and day

  Scenario: Backup and vacuum operations are auditable
    Given the backup and vacuum operations are performed
    Then all operation details are available in purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log for audit purposes

  Scenario: Backup operation is incremental if specified
    Given the backup type is set to "incremental"
    And only records with creation_date > last backup date exist
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then only new or changed records are written to "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with the correct record_count

  Scenario: Backup operation is full if specified
    Given the backup type is set to "full"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all records from purgo_playground.customer_360_raw are written to "/Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup"
    And the backup log table purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log contains a record with the correct record_count
